## Changed

**The Publish page shows a URL change as one renamed entry.** It used to show one removed and one added entry, with every field marked as changed. Now the comparison lists only the fields that changed, usually only the URL. A rename is recognised by its content, as Git recognises one: the old and the new version must agree on at least half of their non-empty fields, the URL aside. "Discard" on the row puts the entry back at its old URL.

## Fixed

A URL change no longer breaks the images of the entry. The rename moved the files in the `media/` folder of the entry to the new folder, but the media fields still pointed into the old folder, which the rename deleted. The references now move with the files.

A renamed entry keeps its place in a manually ordered collection. The rename did not update `_order.json`, so the entry dropped to the end of the list. The new slug now takes the place of the old slug.
